to adjust again.\n\nMaybe we can use L1 to cover (2,1) instead of (2,2). But L1 currently passes through (1,1) and (2,2). If we change L1 to line through (1,1) and (2,1), that's vertical (x=1?), no, line through (1,1) and (2,1) is horizontal (slope 0), not allowed. So cannot.\n\nPerhaps we can use L4 to cover (2,1) as well. L4 currently line through (1,4) and (2,2). Could we change L4 to line through (1,4) and (2,1)? Slope = (1-4)/(2-1) = -3, allowed. Equation: y-4 = -3(x-1) => y = -3x + 7. At x=2, y=1 (point (2,1)). So L4 would cover (1,4) and (2,1). Then (2,2) would be uncovered. But (2,2) is covered by L1 (y=x). So okay.\n\nNow check coverage:\n\n- L1: (1,1),(2,2)\n- L2: (1,2),(2,3)\n- L3: (1,3),(3,2)\n- L4: (1,4),(2,1)\n- D: diagonal points (1,5),(2,4),(3,3),(4,2),(5,1)\n\nNow check all points:\n\nColumn 1: (1,1) L1, (1,2) L2, (1,3) L3, (1,4) L4, (1,5) D. Good.\n\nColumn 2: (2,1) L4, (2,2) L1, (2,3) L2, (2,4) D. Good.\n\nColumn 3: (3,1) ??? Not covered. (3,2) L3, (3,3) D. So (3,1) uncovered.\n\nColumn 4: (4,1) D, (4,2) D. Good.\n\nColumn 5: (5,1) D.\n\nThus only (3,1) remains uncovered. We need to cover (3,1). Could we adjust L2 or L3 to also cover (3,1)? Let's see.\n\nL2 currently line through (1,2) and (2,3). Equation: slope = 1, y = x+1. At x=3, y=4, not (3,1). So not.\n\nL3 currently line through (1,3) and (3,2). Equation: slope = -0.5, y = -0.5x + 3.5. At x=3, y = -1.5 + 3.5 = 2, not (3,1). So not.\n\nWe could try to change L2 to line through (1,2) and (3,1). That slope = (1-2)/(3-1) = -1/2, allowed. That line would also pass through (2,? ) at x=2, y = -0.5*2 + (2+? Actually compute: using points (1,2) and (3,1): slope -0.5, equation y-2 = -0.5(x-1) => y = -0.5x + 2.5. At x=2, y = -1 + 2.5 = 1.5, not integer. So L2 would cover (1,2) and (3,1). Good. Then (2,3) would be uncovered. But we could cover (2,3) with L3 perhaps? L3 currently covers (1,3) and (3,2). Could we adjust L3 to also cover (2,3)? Let's see line through (1,3) and (2,3) is horizontal (slope 0